WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.693
Evidence collection needs organization.

2
00:00:02.693 --> 00:00:14.289
Teams often work from evidence request lists, artifact owners, repositories, naming conventions, version tracking, review status, approval workflows, and collection schedules.

3
00:00:14.289 --> 00:00:28.428
The mechanics matter because assessment and monitoring depend on being able to locate the right artifact, understand what it represents, and determine whether it is current and complete enough for the question being asked.

4
00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:31.196
Artifact ownership is a practical control.

5
00:00:31.196 --> 00:00:38.752
Someone should be responsible for producing, maintaining, explaining, and refreshing each important evidence type.

6
00:00:38.752 --> 00:00:41.595
Engineering may own configuration outputs.

7
00:00:41.595 --> 00:00:44.812
Security may own scan results or incident records.

8
00:00:44.812 --> 00:00:48.478
Operations may own backup checks or monitoring evidence.

9
00:00:48.478 --> 00:00:51.171
Compliance may coordinate review status.

10
00:00:51.171 --> 00:00:57.904
Without owners, evidence often becomes stale, scattered, or difficult to explain under review pressure.

11
00:00:57.904 --> 00:01:01.794
Sensitive evidence handling deserves deliberate planning.

12
00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:12.717
Evidence may contain vulnerability details, network architecture, identities, security tooling, customer information, incident records, or operational weaknesses.

13
00:01:12.717 --> 00:01:19.450
Repositories should use access control, appropriate retention, version history, and review workflows.

14
00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:30.447
Teams should understand which artifacts can be broadly shared, which require tighter handling, and how to provide evidence without exposing unnecessary sensitive detail.

15
00:01:30.447 --> 00:01:33.814
Evidence should be prepared for multiple audiences.

16
00:01:33.814 --> 00:01:36.208
Assessors need to evaluate controls.

17
00:01:36.208 --> 00:01:38.452
Reviewers need to understand risk.

18
00:01:38.452 --> 00:01:41.445
Engineers need to confirm technical accuracy.

19
00:01:41.445 --> 00:01:45.110
Compliance teams need to manage status and traceability.

20
00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:51.395
Good evidence management makes artifacts understandable without relying on one person's memory.

21
00:01:51.395 --> 00:01:59.998
It preserves context, source, date, owner, control relationship, and review status so stakeholders can use the evidence efficiently.
